WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:01.376
It was irresponsible.

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:02.252
Irresponsible?

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:03.128
Absolutely.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:08.049
They spent what, a trillion dollars
plus countless man hours.

00:00:08.049 --> 00:00:11.970
Not to mention political capital,
trying to get one dude back from Mars.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.305
Political capital? It united the world.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.850
Yeah, for a hot second.
But, what if they failed?

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.518
Everyone would have been like,
um excuse me.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.395
You know, there are
people dying here, right?

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:22.522
People are always dying on Earth.
You can't change that.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:25.066
But if you get the opportunity
to bring back Matt Damon.

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:26.776
No, screw Matt Damon.

00:00:26.943 --> 00:00:28.194
That's just harsh!

00:00:28.486 --> 00:00:31.406
Dude, it costs an average of
$1,200 to save a life.

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:32.198
12, what?

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:33.450
When you give money to charity,

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.493
the ones that are
actually going to save lives

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:37.620
are the ones that clean water and
give out medicine and stuff, right?

00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:40.040
Matt Damon's charity
literally cleans water.

00:00:40.081 --> 00:00:41.916
So when you factor in
administrative costs

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:44.294
and how many people would
actually die without help,

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:46.337
that works out to
1,200 bucks per life.

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:50.050
Okay, so what you're saying is
you take a trillion and divide it by 1,200

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:55.430
and you can save 833 million
people's lives on Earth?

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:57.432
You just do that math right now?

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.225
I'm wicked smaht.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:00:59.768
I know.

00:00:59.768 --> 00:01:03.063
It's just you look, like, so dumb.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:04.355
Okay.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.067
Checkmate.

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:09.944
Dang.

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:10.653
Boom.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:13.490
Okay.

00:01:28.546 --> 00:01:30.924
You really don't think
they're sending anybody to save us?

00:01:33.843 --> 00:01:34.886
I mean,

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:38.640
I'm sure they're doing what they can.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.558
Within reason.

